{% block demo_examples %}
## Examples

### Basic
<DemoWidget cmd={`stream.step_sankey()`} path="/docs-demos/widgets/step-sankey/basic.html" height={560} />

### Path pattern - central event
A single event as `path_pattern` re-centers the diagram on that event instead of
`path_start`: column 0 is always `purchase`, negative columns are the steps
leading up to it, positive columns are what follows.

<DemoWidget cmd={`stream.step_sankey(path_pattern="purchase")`} path="/docs-demos/widgets/step-sankey/path_pattern_central.html" height={660} />

### Path pattern - funnel patterns
Chaining several anchors with `.*` renders one diagram block per anchor, side by side,
so you can follow a multi-step funnel across blocks.

<DemoWidget cmd={`stream.step_sankey(path_pattern="payment_details->.*->shipping_details->.*->purchase", step_window=2)`} path="/docs-demos/widgets/step-sankey/path_pattern_funnel.html" height={660} sidebarOpen={false} />

### Path pattern - drop-off points
`path_pattern="path_end"` centers on where paths end, so the columns to the left show
what users tend to do right before dropping off (or completing their path).

<DemoWidget cmd={`stream.step_sankey(path_pattern="path_end")`} path="/docs-demos/widgets/step-sankey/path_pattern_dropoff.html" height={660} />

